WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:05.000
Once shooting wraps on a movie, props usually
get packed up for the next film, auctioned

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.240
off for charity, or given to a museum.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:11.860
But sometimes, actors just take the props
from the set for themselves, with no one the

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:12.860
wiser.

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:16.370
Whether for sentimental reasons or because
they feel their acting deserves a more tangible

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:20.330
reward than a paycheck, there are plenty of
famous actors who have admitted to nicking

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:24.380
some valuable, and not so valuable, props
once shooting was finished.

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:28.800
Here are some of the props that actors stole
from the sets of their movies.

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:30.000
Locket up

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.989
After the final film of the Hunger Games franchise,
Mockingjay: Part 2, was released, a few of

00:00:34.989 --> 00:00:38.620
the main actors revealed that they had taken
some props home over the years.

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:43.080
Considering Josh Hutcherson played the perpetually
romantic Peeta, what he admitted to stealing

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:44.530
is actually quite sweet.

00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:49.780
"I took home in Catching Fire the locket that
Peeta gives to Katniss that has the 3 pictures

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:50.780
in it, I took that one home."

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:54.309
Meanwhile, Jennifer Lawrence took home some
pieces of her character's amazing outfits.

00:00:54.309 --> 00:00:57.609
"I have the leather jacket, the leather hunting
jacket."

00:00:57.609 --> 00:01:00.469
"And my leather, um, hunting boots."

00:01:00.469 --> 00:01:05.110
Unlike his co-stars, Liam Hemsworth claims
he didn't take part in any thievery.

00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:06.880
So what did he leave the set with?

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:10.270
"Lots of memories and good friendships, that's
what I took."

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:11.610
Hammer home

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:15.320
While Liam might be surprisingly good-hearted
when it comes to not stealing things from

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:18.030
set, his brother certainly isn't as innocent.

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:21.941
Chris Hemsworth has kept a memento of every
single time he's been called upon to play

00:01:21.941 --> 00:01:23.911
the God of Thunder in the Marvel Cinematic
Universe.

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:25.500
"Did you steal a hammer at least?

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:26.340
Did you take a hammer home?"

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:26.840
"A few, yeah."

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:27.840
"Oh, a few?

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:29.460
How many hammers do you have?"

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.000
"About five."

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:34.700
One of those hammers is on permanent display
in, well, his bathroom.

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:37.750
"It's next to the toilet, if you need some
assistance with that for whatever reason...:"

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:41.040
"So it's like a toilet paper holder, like
a very expensive…"

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:42.480
"It is now!"

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:44.850
Bella Swan, jewelry thief

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:49.810
Kristen Stewart was only 17 years old while
filming the first Twilight movie and 22 when

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:54.340
the final film, Breaking Dawn Part 2, was
released to theaters.

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:57.350
While her vampire love, Robert Pattinson,
and the rest of the cast reportedly don't

00:01:57.350 --> 00:02:01.550
seem to have many fond memories of filming,
Stewart appears to have more of a soft spot

00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:02.740
for the franchise.

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:06.970
She told People magazine that she kept some
jewelry that Bella Swan wears in the film

00:02:06.970 --> 00:02:11.470
to better remember director Catherine Hardwicke
and co-star Robert Pattinson.

00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:12.470
Stewart admitted,

00:02:12.470 --> 00:02:13.550
"I kept the rings.

00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:15.940
The rings are really important to me."

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:18.000
Unconventional desires

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:22.000
If there's any movie that depends on its props,
it would probably have to be 50 Shades of

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.000
Grey.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:27.200
The franchise became a box-office smash and
made Dakota Johnson and Jamie Dornan almost

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:29.840
as wealthy and famous as the characters they
played.

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:34.660
But according to Marie Claire, Johnson took
something else home besides her massive paycheck,

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:37.250
one of the floggers from Christian Grey's
secret room.

00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:41.690
She made sure to specify that it's just gathering
dust in her garage, which seems like a very

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:45.610
different use for the item than Christian
Grey would have for it.

00:02:45.610 --> 00:02:47.410
Live long and pilfer

00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:51.310
Simon Pegg has been pretty open about his
humble, nerdy beginnings, and at this point

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:54.980
he's definitely made it as a geeky lad living
out his dream jobs.

00:02:54.980 --> 00:03:00.330
He appeared in 2009's Star Trek reboot and
reprised the role for the sequel, Star Trek:

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:01.530
Into Darkness.

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:06.880
According to Female First, Pegg finally accomplished
a long-time childhood goal by keeping a Starfleet

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:08.620
badge while filming the sequel.

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:10.470
"This is my Starfleet insignia."

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:14.850
Despite tight security, Pegg admitted that
he was able to slip the badge into his bag

00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:16.460
without anyone noticing.

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:17.320
"It's kinda cool."

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:20.120
Secretly Slytherin

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:24.960
Daniel Radcliffe was only 11 years old when
he started filming Harry Potter and the Sorcerer's

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:28.569
Stone, and he continued to star in the franchise
for nearly ten years.

00:03:28.569 --> 00:03:32.540
Considering he spent most of his childhood
providing childhood memories for other kids,

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:36.709
it makes sense that Radcliffe would want a
souvenir of his time spent on set, even if

00:03:36.709 --> 00:03:38.070
he had to steal one.

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:42.209
That souvenir turned out to be a couple of
pairs of glasses that Harry Potter wears;

00:03:42.209 --> 00:03:46.160
one from the first movie and one from The
Deathly Hallows Part 1.

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:49.870
It's a sweet reminder of the time he spent
on set, but you'd think he would've gone with

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:50.730
a wand, right?

